From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sat, 4 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: a turn cut short by the loss of its turn player fires
 its End Phase event for the others at n > 2

When the turn player is eliminated in its own turn, PhaseEvent(PHASE_END) skipped its whole step 0 (force_turn_end) but
still ran reset_phase, so every RESET_PHASE turn count counted the cut-short turn while the EVENT_PHASE+PHASE_END effects
never fired for it. Nightmare's Steelcage (own counter +1 in its End Phase effect, reset after 2 opponent turns) lost both
effects with the counter at 1 and was never destroyed.

Rule (ADR 0002, elimination): a turn cut short by an elimination counts as an ended turn for every turn count. The End
Phase event now runs for the living duelists: forced triggers and continuous effects, with hand_adjusted set so that no
optional effect and no free chain window is offered. A genuine EFFECT_SKIP_EP still skips it.

Guarded with n_duelists > 2 and a turn player that is not alive. With 2 duelists (and the Tag relay) nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
---
 processor.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/processor.cpp b/processor.cpp
index dd1fe45..7bd6d6c 100644
--- a/processor.cpp
+++ b/processor.cpp
@@ -325,11 +325,18 @@ bool field::process(Processors::PhaseEvent& arg) {
 	auto phase = arg.phase;
 	switch(arg.step) {
 	case 0: {
+		// n > 2 (ADR 0002, elimination): a turn cut short by the loss of its turn player counts as an ended turn for every turn
+		// count (RESET_*_TURN, "until the end of the Nth turn"), so its End Phase event is not skipped: the forced and the
+		// continuous effects of the living duelists run. hand_adjusted keeps the optional effects and the free chain out, and
+		// the hand limit has nothing to discard (the cards of the seat that lost are gone). A genuine skip of the End Phase stays.
+		const bool out_turn = n_duelists > 2 && phase == PHASE_END && core.force_turn_end && !is_alive(infos.turn_player);
+		if(out_turn)
+			core.hand_adjusted = true;
 		if((phase == PHASE_DRAW && (core.force_turn_end || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_SKIP_DP)))
 				|| (phase == PHASE_STANDBY && (core.force_turn_end || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_SKIP_SP)))
 				|| (phase == PHASE_BATTLE_START && (core.force_turn_end || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_SKIP_BP)))
 				|| (phase == PHASE_BATTLE && (core.force_turn_end || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_SKIP_BP)))
-				|| (phase == PHASE_END && (core.force_turn_end || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_SKIP_EP)))) {
+				|| (phase == PHASE_END && ((core.force_turn_end && !out_turn) || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_SKIP_EP)))) {
 			arg.step = 24;
 			return FALSE;
 		}
